# Landing page

## Deploy

- Root for Vercel: `web/` (see `web/vercel.json`, `web/README.md`)
- Static HTML/CSS/JS — no frontend build step
- Local preview: `npm run landing` or `python -m http.server 4000 --directory web`

## Key files

- `web/index.html` — hero, waitlist, `#demo` interactive section, inline JSON-LD `@graph`, inline GA4 gtag (`G-88L32JZQDH`; CSP hash in `web/vercel.json`)
- `web/demo.js` — IIFE with dummy data (`STATS`, `SPOTLIGHT_GAMES`); mirrors app UX, no app imports
- `web/demo.css` — demo dashboard chrome
- `web/main.js` — waitlist POST to `/api/subscribe`
- `web/free-claims.json` — built by `build_free_claims.py` at repo root
- `web/mirror/` — Pro cloud library viewer (`/mirror`); separate from marketing page chrome

FAQ JSON-LD must match the `#faq` details list: `npm run check:landing-seo`.

Attended OpenSEO / GSC / GA playbook: `.cursor/rules/seo-operator.mdc`.

## Serverless

- `web/api/subscribe.js` — waitlist (Resend + optional Supabase)
- `web/api/report.js` — opt-in bug reports from local app

## Keep in sync

See **AGENTS.md hard rule 6** for the canonical full sync-pair list. Landing-specific:

- `web/marquee-speed.js` ↔ `js/marquee-speed.js` (duplicate IIFE vs ESM)
- Sample covers: `web/assets/sample/*.{webp,png}` (fictional games)
- Demo stats in `demo.js` are independent from app state — update both if changing marketing numbers

## Copy conventions

- **No em dashes or AI tells in marketing copy.** Never use `—` (em dash, U+2014) in any front-facing string in `web/` (hero, demo text, `sponsors.json`, email copy in `api/subscribe.js`). Use a spaced hyphen (` - `) or rephrase. Also avoid LLM-flavored marketing (contrast frames, hype verbs, empty intensifiers, abstract positioning, verbatim claim repetition across sections). Code comments are exempt. See AGENTS.md hard rule 8.
